. 
.                 * where ihs_income_gap is the dependent variable, daughters_n
> r is the number of daughters, 
.                 * `controls' is the vector of control variables, absorb(tot_k
> ids) includes total children fixed 
.                 * effects, and cluster(hid) adjusts standard errors for withi
> n-household correlation over time.  
.                 * 
.                 * Interpretation of Results:  
.                 * The primary coefficient of interest is that on daughters_nr
> . A negative and statistically 
.                 * significant coefficient would indicate that having more dau
> ghters is associated with a smaller 
.                 * income gap, suggesting more equal economic contributions wi
> thin households. Statistical 
.                 * significance will be evaluated at the 10%, 5%, and 1% level
> s, with t-statistics reported. 
.                 * Residual degrees of freedom are reported as appropriate for
>  OLS estimation. 
.                 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[daughters_nr]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[daughters_nr]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local t_value = _b[daughters_nr] / _se[daughters_nr]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`t_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[daughters_nr]

.                 local interpretation "negative coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
